<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sipahi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The sipahis were cavalrymen of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> who held land grants called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timar">timars</a>, from which they collected revenue in return for military service. They formed a core of the Ottoman army in its classical period. Accounts of the Ottoman Empire describe their role in the Ottoman socioeconomic system.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sipahi.jpg" alt="Sipahi" width="311" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dal Mehmed Çelebi (Asafi) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Secaatname_0179_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
